# Hey there 👋

You might have found this site from Google, some [code](http://github.com/featherbear/) I wrote, my [UNSW course notes](/blog/post/unsw/)... or maybe you're a robot?  
Either way, welcome!

During the week I work as a Security Engineer at [Atlassian](https://www.atlassian.com).  
During the weekend, I do wedding photography and event production stuff, or catch up on sleep!

The rest of my life is basically a mixture of software, audio, lighting, video, photos, computer networks, and security.

I studied Computer Engineering at the [University of New South Wales](https://unsw.edu.au) in Sydney, Australia.  
Formerly I did Electrical Engineering, but I eventually found myself more fascinated with hardware design (and I hate maths).  
I wrote a [thesis](https://featherbear.cc/UNSW-CSE-Thesis/) about hacking into robotic vacuum cleaners, if you want to read that!

---

# My life, sort of categorised..

## 💻 [Hardware & Software](/programming)

> I make and break things - though mainly the latter...

My interests lie in network technologies, multimedia systems and dev o(o)ps - though realistically the reason I write software is so that I don't have to pay for them.  

I also supposedly do something involved with cyber security, but let's keep that a ... `c2VjcmV0==` ... between you and me 🕵️‍♀️

## 📸 [Photography](https://www.instagram.com/_andrewjwong/)

> “Alright on three... three!”

When I'm not doing wedding photography, you can probably find me standing in the exact same spot for hours upon hours capturing the landscapes.  
_That, or..._ looking like a lunatic carrying around a bunch of random lights for some creative portraits or light paintings.  

## 🎬 [Audio / Visual Production](/blog/categories/audio-visual/)  

> “Camera 2, iris up.” × “Is this thing on?”

I'm one of those people who you don't know exist, until we mess up.  

Whilst there's no hope for me in front of a camera or microphone, I can sure make the talent look and sound good!  
From corporate events like conferences, to weddings, to concerts, theatre and festivals - I mainly work as a live sound engineer (mixing audio) and broadcast engineer (video production and livestreaming), but basically I'm a _"jack of all trades, master of <s>none</s> some"_.  

I also do some local systems integrations for churches and venues, if you need help with that..

## 🎸 Music

When I was younger I was forced to learn piano, then I was forced to learn clarinet, and then I was forced to learn saxophone.  
I don't remember how to play any of them, but these days I own an unhealthy number of guitars..

## 🤷‍♀️ Misc

Sports? Table Tennis, and going on hikes/walks (if you consider that a sport...)  
Sleep deprived? Absolutely.  
Hotel? Trivago.

Favourite Emoji: 🔥

